hypotheses.statement:
For every fixed $k\ge1$ and every sufficiently large fixed $r$, $$\label{intro:bond-arm-exponents}
 \pi_1(R)=R^{-5/48+o(1)},\qquad
 \pi_{2k}(r,R)=R^{-(4k^2-1)/12+o(1)}
 \qquad(R\to\infty).$$

In any fixed buffered annulus or sector of the preceding types, a raw passage count $X$ satisfies $$\label{prelim:passage-moment}
 \mathbb E[\exp(BX)\mid\text{exterior}]\le C_B
 \qquad(0\le B<\infty),$$ uniformly in scale and in exterior states inducing the specified graph and arbitrary boundary partition.

With the definitions above, $$\begin{aligned}
 2P+2D_*+4(C_0+C_1)&\le o(\log n),\label{exp:rectangle-budget}\\
 C_0+C_1+L_0+L_1&\le o(\log n),\label{exp:corner-budget}\\
 P+\sum_j\log\frac{F_-(a_j)}{F_+(a_j)}
   &\le o(\log n),\label{exp:charge-budget}
\end{aligned}$$ where the finite list of fixed charges in the last inequality satisfies <a href="#exp:charge-range" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="exp:charge-range">[exp:charge-range]</a> and $\sum_j a_j=1$.

For every bounded function $\gamma$ of the two colors and every boundary point $u$ distinct from the four marks, $$\lim_{z\to u}\limsup_{n\to\infty}
 \left|\mathbb E_{\rm open}
       [\gamma(\operatorname{col}(V(z)))D_{V(z)}]\right|=0.
 \label{four:boundary-residual}$$ Here $z$ in the outer limit is a macroscopic interior location, and any lattice vertices tending to it may be used in the inner limit.

For sufficiently large fixed $L$, under the exterior positive tilt $
u_U\propto U\mu$, $$\mathbb E_{
u_U}(Y/U)\ge c_L>0,\qquad
 \mathbb E_{
u_U}|Y/U|^p\le C_{p,L}
 \label{wall:distant-moments}$$ for every fixed $p>0$, uniformly for large $R_0$ and fine mesh.

On every compact capacity interval, the Dobrushin driving functions converge in law, uniformly, to $\sqrt\kappa B_t$, where $B$ is standard Brownian motion and $$\label{chordal:kappa}
 \kappa=\frac{8}{1+h}
        =\frac{4\pi}{\arccos(-\sqrt q/2)}.$$

Away from $\theta\in\{0,2\pi\}$, every limiting branch has the local characteristics $$\label{tree:sde}
 \begin{aligned}
 dW_t&=\sqrt\kappa\,dB_t+
          \frac{6-\kappa}{2}\cot(\theta_t/2)\,dt,\\
 dO_t&=\cot(\theta_t/2)\,dt,\qquad \theta_t=O_t-W_t.
 \end{aligned}$$ Here $t$ is that branch’s radial clock; the martingale identities hold relative to the full causal exploration history.

In its own radial clock, the limiting gap is the unique instantaneous reflected diffusion on $[0,2\pi]$ with interior generator $$\label{tree:generator}
 \mathcal A f(\theta)=\frac\kappa2 f''(\theta)
       +\frac{\kappa-4}{2}\cot(\theta/2)f'(\theta).$$

