Let $\psi:D\to\mathbb H$ send $a,c,d$ to $0,1,\infty$, and put $x=\psi(b)\in(0,1)$. Under the boundary and approximation conventions above, $$\label{intro:cardy-formula}
 \lim_{n\to\infty}\mathbb P(C_n)
 =\frac{\displaystyle\int_0^x[t(1-t)]^{-2/3}\,\mathrm dt}
        {\displaystyle\int_0^1[t(1-t)]^{-2/3}\,\mathrm dt}.$$

